---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Legal" description="Logic Planet is proprietary software. Copyright © 2026 Rubble Software.">
  <article class="shell pt-12 text-center sm:pt-16 lg:pt-20">
    <h1 class="section-label m-0">Legal</h1>
    <h2 class="mx-auto m-0 mt-6 max-w-2xl font-display text-[clamp(1.75rem,3vw,2.25rem)] leading-none tracking-[-0.03em]">
      Copyright &amp; Usage Notice
    </h2>

    <div class="mx-auto mt-10 max-w-2xl border-t border-line pt-8">
      <p class="m-0 text-[1.125rem] leading-7 text-ink">Logic Planet © 2026 Rubble Software. All rights reserved.</p>

      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-col gap-6 text-[1.0625rem] leading-7 text-muted">
        <p class="m-0">
          Logic Planet is proprietary software currently in pre-alpha development. It is not open-source software. Access
          to the game does not grant permission to redistribute, repackage, sell, or commercially exploit the game, its
          source code, or its proprietary assets.
        </p>
        <p class="m-0">
          The game is currently made available for personal, non-commercial use. Its development, distribution,
          licensing, and monetization model may change at any time as the project evolves.
        </p>
        <p class="m-0">
          <strong class="font-medium text-ink">Future commercialization is possible.</strong> Logic Planet may become a
          paid product or introduce other commercial licensing models in the future. Pre-alpha access does not guarantee
          that the game, future releases, or all features will remain free.
        </p>
        <p class="m-0">
          Features, availability, and distribution arrangements may change throughout development. No guarantee is made
          regarding a release date, continued availability, or the final form of the project.
        </p>
        <p class="m-0">All rights not expressly granted are reserved by Rubble Software or the applicable rights holders.</p>
        <p class="m-0">
          By downloading or using Logic Planet, you acknowledge that it is proprietary software provided under limited
          usage permissions, not an open-source project.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p class="m-0 mt-10 border-t border-line pt-6 text-[1.0625rem] leading-7 text-ink">
        Logic Planet is an independent project. Copyright © 2026 Rubble Software. All rights reserved.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
